## Interface: 16001, 16002, 16003, 16100, 16101, 16200
## Title: Quiet Professions
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\Trade_BlackSmithing
## Notes: The cheapest way to level a profession from where you are, reckoned from today's prices rather than a guide's: every recipe weighed against what's in your bags and bank, what the auction house asks listing by listing, and which recipes you know, with the gear worth making for your characters put in on the way. /qprof opens the route, what to buy for it (with a two-press Buy at the auction house, and what your other characters should mail you: they get a Mail list of it, and can do the buying for you), the gear (for a cook: the food that suits your class), the plans worth getting and what sells; for a miner, what smelting earns (your ore as it is or as bars, and ore worth buying to smelt). Nothing is made for you, and nothing bought without your press. A tool a recipe needs (an enchanter's runed rod, an engineer's spanner) is on the route once, before the first step that needs it; the basic ones (a smith's hammer, flint and tinder) count as yours. For Blacksmithing, Tailoring, Leatherworking, Engineering, Enchanting, Alchemy, Mining, Cooking and First Aid. Its settings are in Options, AddOns, Quiet. Your bank and other characters are counted by any Quiet addon they have on; better still with Quiet Auctions (its price scans).
